{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DnC89ZVfeCuZdR6h8ajegF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand the current state and determine what tasks to propose.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It's an experiment in specification-driven development using an AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/<name>/` - One directory per utility (main.go + tests)\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing framework\n- `pkg/sys/` - System calls\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n\n\n- `pkg/hashutil/` - Hash/checksum utilities\n- `pkg/sizeparse/` - Size parsing\n- `pkg/encutil/` - Encoding utilities\n- `docs/specs/` - SRDs, use cases, test suites\n- `magefiles/` - Build automation\n\n**Current State**: Looking at the code status and requirement states, release 00.0 is partially complete with magefiles, sys, hashutil, sizeparse, and encutil implemented while format and testutils haven't been started yet. Release 01.1 (cat) is not started, 01.2 (sponge) is implemented, and 01.3 appears to be cut off in the list.\n\nContinuing through the releases, I see 02.0 (true, false, yes, basename, dirname) is fully implemented, 02.1 (tee) is done, and 02.2 (head, seq) is implemented. Release 03.0 (wc) is complete, while 03.1 has partial progress with nproc not started but the others done. Release 04.0 (ls, ls-extended) hasn't been started, 04.1 is partially done with logname not started, and 05.0 shows partial progress with echo and tac not started but nl and fold implemented. Beyond that, many releases are still not started.\n\nNow I'm examining the requirement states to see which requirements are marked as complete or in progress. ready to check which SRDs have requirements ready:\n\nLooking at the requirement_states