{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DnC89ZVfeCuZdR6h8ajegF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. It stress-tests a specification-driven AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator).\n\n**Architecture**: `cmd/<name>/` per utility with main.go and differential tests. Shared libraries: `pkg/testutils/` (diff test harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscalls), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/hashutil/`, `pkg/sizeparse/`, `pkg/encutil/`. Build via `magefiles/`. Specs in `docs/specs/`.\n\n**Current state**: Many utilities are implemented. The most recent commits completed the `cmd/unexpand` contract (#5272) and R1.1-R1.4 implementation (#5273). The requirement_states show remaining ready requirements across many SRDs, with srd025-unexpand (rel05.1) being the earliest with R2.1-R4.4 still ready.\n\n**Current release**: rel05.1 (expand/unexpand). Expand is not in requirement_states (presumably complete). Unexpand has R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.3, R4.1-R4.4 remaining. After rel05.1, the next release is rel05.2 (cut, paste).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nEarliest incomplete release with ready requirements: **rel05.1** (srd025-unexpand R2.1-R4.4). After completing unexpand, rel05.2 (srd026-cut, srd027-paste) is next. With a 4-task budget: finish unexpand (3 tasks) + start cut contract (1 task).\n\n**Dependencies**: Unexpand tasks are sequential (modify same files). Cut contract is independent.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification (Step 3b)\n\n```\nTask 0: srd025-unexpand R2.1(w=1), R2.2(w=1), R2.3(w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 1: srd025-unexpand R3.1(w=1), R3.2(w=1), R3.3(w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1 = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 2: srd025-unexpand R4.1(w=1), R4.2(w=1), R4.3(w=1), R4.4(w=1)\nTotal weight: 1+1+1+1 = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n\nTask 3: srd026-cut contract (no SRD sub-requirements consumed; creates stubs only)\nTotal weight: 0 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/unexpand: implement srd025-unexpand R2.1-R2.3\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd025-unexpand.yaml (full SRD -- implement requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/unexpand/main.go (existing implementation from R1.1-R1.4 contract and first task)\n      - cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework -- BuildBinary, RunDiffTests, DiffTest)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality required by srd025-unexpand R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n      - path: cmd/unexpand/unexpand_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases covering R2.1, R2.2, R2.3\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.1 exactly as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.2 exactly as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd025-unexpand requirement R2.3 exactly as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern -- use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") to compile cmd/unexpand and testutils.RunDiffTests to compare against the reference binary\n      - id: D2\n        text: Reference binary is gunexpand from Homebrew GNU coreutils -- use exec.LookPath(\"gunexpand\") and t.Skip if not found\n      - id: D3\n        text: All differential test cases must set LC_ALL=C in the Env field to ensure deterministic locale behavior\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: srd025-unexpand requirements R2.1, R2.2, and R2.3 are fully implemented in cmd/unexpand/main.go\n      - id: AC2\n   